  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Overlap – pass or dummy",
  "description": "Five against five on about 40 × 30 metres. At one end is a full-size goal with a goalkeeper from the team defending it; at the other end two cone goals without a goalkeeper, where goals are scored by dribbling through. Swap at half-time so both teams attack the big goal.\n\nThe team on the ball creates overlaps anywhere on the pitch, including in tight spaces near goal. A goal after an overlap is worth two points – both when the overlapping player got the ball and when the player on the ball used the overlap to dummy the pass and go alone. Other goals are worth one.\n\nVariation: three points if the overlap ends with a pass to a third player. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The player on the ball dribbles inside and takes the defender along – that opens the space outside."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The overlapping player runs behind the ball carrier, at full speed, and calls."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Read the defender: if they stay with you, pass. If they follow the runner, dummy and go yourself."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Play the ball ahead of the overlapping player so the run never has to stop."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
